<title>UK: Czech Export Bank bond due Thursday - bankers.</title>
<headline>Czech Export Bank bond due Thursday - bankers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech Export Bank (CEB) $150 million five-year bond is due to be launched next Thursday, bankers said on Friday.</p>
<p>J.P. Morgan will underwrite the transaction.</p>
<p>Spread talk is around the low 50 basis point area over U.S. Treasury notes.</p>
<p>In April CEB said it expected to issue a $200-300 million, five-year Eurobond by the end of May, but now seems to have opted for a smaller-sized deal.</p>
<p>The CEB was established in 1995 with a business mandate to increase Czech exports by providing exporters with competitive financing.</p>
<p>-- Hayley Pienaar, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7718</p>
</text>
